(3463352, 483299, 6999, '<td valign="top">One always feels that dark images benefit better from the use of grain - simply because it was always high speed film where one saw that, I''m sure. The negative space seems a touch overwhelming here, and the title and suggestions of the pose ... well, a little pretentious I''m afraid. The light on the wall is effective though, suggestive of prison, of captivity.</td>', 'One always feels that dark images benefit better from the use of grain - simply because it was always high speed film where one saw that, I''m sure. The negative space seems a touch overwhelming here, and the title and suggestions of the pose ... well, a little pretentious I''m afraid. The light on the wall is effective though, suggestive of prison, of captivity.', '2007-03-15 05:58:42.000000', NULL, 1),
