(3464225, 481080, 22748, '<td valign="top">Strong Bad says: Holy crap! Awesome image. I love the contrasty look and the way the lines of the dock recede into the distance before ending. The texture of the clouds is fascinating and the glowing sun makes a great silhouette and projects a subtle but effective shadow on the ground. The textures of the rough water and the dock surface, combined with the varying textures of the clouds, make an extremely visually interesting image. By silhouetting the person, there is no distracting detail there, and the monotone nature of the image eliminates the distraction of color. The grain is not overwhelming, just slightly apparent in the sky mostly, and complexity of all the textures in the image coordinate perfectly with the grain in such a way that the viewer doesn''t become conscious of the grain.</td>', 'Strong Bad says: Holy crap! Awesome image. I love the contrasty look and the way the lines of the dock recede into the distance before ending. The texture of the clouds is fascinating and the glowing sun makes a great silhouette and projects a subtle but effective shadow on the ground. The textures of the rough water and the dock surface, combined with the varying textures of the clouds, make an extremely visually interesting image. By silhouetting the person, there is no distracting detail there, and the monotone nature of the image eliminates the distraction of color. The grain is not overwhelming, just slightly apparent in the sky mostly, and complexity of all the textures in the image coordinate perfectly with the grain in such a way that the viewer doesn''t become conscious of the grain.', '2007-03-15 13:34:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(3464226, 483249, 74664, '<td valign="top">less grain would make it better IMO</td>', 'less grain would make it better IMO', '2007-03-15 13:34:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(3464232, 481914, 73564, '<td valign="top">Damn~COOL</td>', 'Damn~COOL', '2007-03-15 13:36:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(3464246, 481959, 22748, '<td valign="top">I like the image; by keeping a shallow DOF you have focus attention on the subject and eliminated distracting elements from the composition. However, the bits of horizontal banding, particularly about 1/5th of the way down from the top of the image, is kind of distracting. But still a good image.</td>', 'I like the image; by keeping a shallow DOF you have focus attention on the subject and eliminated distracting elements from the composition. However, the bits of horizontal banding, particularly about 1/5th of the way down from the top of the image, is kind of distracting. But still a good image.', '2007-03-15 13:40:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(3464253, 483923, 74664, '<td valign="top">Love the message, maybe a bit too grainy though.</td>', 'Love the message, maybe a bit too grainy though.', '2007-03-15 13:43:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(3464256, 483991, 22748, '<td valign="top">This is a fabulous image. The only thing I don''t like is the grain. It looks kind of like sensor noise that has been compressed and processed: it seems rather coarse but it also has extreme variations in amplitude. I love the composition, however, it is a great portrait.</td>', 'This is a fabulous image. The only thing I don''t like is the grain. It looks kind of like sensor noise that has been compressed and processed: it seems rather coarse but it also has extreme variations in amplitude. I love the composition, however, it is a great portrait.', '2007-03-15 13:44:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(3464259, 483847, 22748, '<td valign="top">Great use of grain: not excessive and it has an attractive quality. Please let us know in the photograph description what technique you used for the grain, I am interested in looking back at the entries after the challenge and finding out what techniques provide attractive grain vs. ugly, noisy digital-looking patterns.</td>', 'Great use of grain: not excessive and it has an attractive quality. Please let us know in the photograph description what technique you used for the grain, I am interested in looking back at the entries after the challenge and finding out what techniques provide attractive grain vs. ugly, noisy digital-looking patterns.', '2007-03-15 13:46:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(3464264, 483758, 23484, '<td valign="top">Nice shot.  Good composition and use of grain.</td>', 'Nice shot.  Good composition and use of grain.', '2007-03-15 13:48:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(3464269, 483814, 23484, '<td valign="top">Great shot. I think you made a great choice for the challenge.  The compositon and contrast is great. I would like to see just a tad more grain.</td>', 'Great shot. I think you made a great choice for the challenge.  The compositon and contrast is great. I would like to see just a tad more grain.', '2007-03-15 13:49:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(3464274, 484011, 22748, '<td valign="top">This one is only OK for me, dawg. There''s just a lot of chroma noise that seems to be in this one, like in the shadows on the platform between the lighted areas.</td>', 'This one is only OK for me, dawg. There''s just a lot of chroma noise that seems to be in this one, like in the shadows on the platform between the lighted areas.', '2007-03-15 13:51:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(3464276, 483412, 74664, '<td valign="top">aww! great picture</td>', 'aww! great picture', '2007-03-15 13:53:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(3464281, 483564, 22748, '<td valign="top">The ''grain'' in this one is very digital-sensor-noise-looking to me. By that I mean, patchy color noise and horizontal/vertical linear artifacts in the noise pattern. The composition itself is rather nice, I do like its simplicity. Perhaps without the noise it would be a really nice image.</td>', 'The ''grain'' in this one is very digital-sensor-noise-looking to me. By that I mean, patchy color noise and horizontal/vertical linear artifacts in the noise pattern. The composition itself is rather nice, I do like its simplicity. Perhaps without the noise it would be a really nice image.', '2007-03-15 13:54:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(3464284, 483528, 74664, '<td valign="top">The foot being so close doesn''t really work IMO.</td>', 'The foot being so close doesn''t really work IMO.', '2007-03-15 13:55:20.000000', NULL, 1),
