(3478689, 481521, 50641, '<td valign="top">I like this.  I''m kinda cursing those anachronistic resin chairs though.  I love what you did with the crop/perspective especially with how the ''roof'' appears - and the placement of the elvis poster is perfect.  The colors are pretty good as is, but if I were experimenting, I might try fooling around with hues, saturation and contrasts to make them even more ''vintage'' looking.  Anyway, this was a great choice of subject for the challenge and deserved a better score.</td>', 'I like this.  I''m kinda cursing those anachronistic resin chairs though.  I love what you did with the crop/perspective especially with how the ''roof'' appears - and the placement of the elvis poster is perfect.  The colors are pretty good as is, but if I were experimenting, I might try fooling around with hues, saturation and contrasts to make them even more ''vintage'' looking.  Anyway, this was a great choice of subject for the challenge and deserved a better score.', '2007-03-21 13:41:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(3478691, 481080, 65547, '<td valign="top">Great work, very well done!</td>', 'Great work, very well done!', '2007-03-21 13:41:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(3478718, 480901, 24212, '<td valign="top">As you mentioned, the grass certainly mimics the angles in the fence. That is the sort of detail that I really like and would have voted highly for (not enough time in the day ATM to do a lot of voting). The grain (I presume it was added post-capture) seems to have given the sky a nice warm feeling, although conversely, I feel that it is a little overpowering, especially as the detail in the ground seems to mask its presence slightly. It could just be my eyes (it probably is), but the grain almost seems to form a halo around the building, too.</td>', 'As you mentioned, the grass certainly mimics the angles in the fence. That is the sort of detail that I really like and would have voted highly for (not enough time in the day ATM to do a lot of voting). The grain (I presume it was added post-capture) seems to have given the sky a nice warm feeling, although conversely, I feel that it is a little overpowering, especially as the detail in the ground seems to mask its presence slightly. It could just be my eyes (it probably is), but the grain almost seems to form a halo around the building, too.', '2007-03-21 13:51:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(3478719, 480710, 50641, '<td valign="top">A bold entry!  You could even zoom in and get more macro on this and it would retain interest.  With a shot of this type, if you wanted to soften the lighting without losing contrast elsewhere (with basic editing), you can try using an warm photo filter and uncheck ''preserve luminosity''.  It''s funny that being this literal with a literal crowd still results in an oobie!  Good for you :)</td>', 'A bold entry!  You could even zoom in and get more macro on this and it would retain interest.  With a shot of this type, if you wanted to soften the lighting without losing contrast elsewhere (with basic editing), you can try using an warm photo filter and uncheck ''preserve luminosity''.  It''s funny that being this literal with a literal crowd still results in an oobie!  Good for you :)', '2007-03-21 13:51:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(3478801, 480689, 69698, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for the votes - this was my 1st entry ever on DPChallenge. Will definitely come back again. <br/> <br/>Regards</td>', 'Thank you all for the votes - this was my 1st entry ever on DPChallenge. Will definitely come back again.  Regards', '2007-03-21 14:29:37.000000', NULL, 0),
