(3479031, 483839, 30982, '<td valign="top">Lovely, Sher - ever so delicate and perfectly lit.</td>', 'Lovely, Sher - ever so delicate and perfectly lit.', '2007-03-21 16:08:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(3479064, 481806, 53316, '<td valign="top">I love the composition and the tones a great deal, as well as your choice of black and white. I think the grain (noise) in the image is nice but doesn''t really add very much to the image''s impact, which is what a lot of voters were looking for in this challenge.</td>', 'I love the composition and the tones a great deal, as well as your choice of black and white. I think the grain (noise) in the image is nice but doesn''t really add very much to the image''s impact, which is what a lot of voters were looking for in this challenge.', '2007-03-21 16:25:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(3479080, 482514, 66201, '<td valign="top">Wow - expected this to be on the top 10 page :-(... <br/> <br/>Ironically your relatively low placing makes me (in my lower placing)feel a bit better: this was SO underrated. Looking at your comments many others saw the mastery of this shot. 7 favourites!!!!! That says it all.</td>', 'Wow - expected this to be on the top 10 page :-(...  Ironically your relatively low placing makes me (in my lower placing)feel a bit better: this was SO underrated. Looking at your comments many others saw the mastery of this shot. 7 favourites!!!!! That says it all.', '2007-03-21 16:31:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(3479089, 481723, 6999, '<td valign="top">But you know how photos of kids tend to get voted here, yes? You hit a nail on the head with this though - anything that gives the sense of needing long exposure - basically, anything that looks like it needed fast film to shoot it - works in our understanding of where photographic grain should be seen. It''s a basic, and nonsensical really, reaction. One might quibble with how far you''ve taken the whites of that dress, but that''s all.</td>', 'But you know how photos of kids tend to get voted here, yes? You hit a nail on the head with this though - anything that gives the sense of needing long exposure - basically, anything that looks like it needed fast film to shoot it - works in our understanding of where photographic grain should be seen. It''s a basic, and nonsensical really, reaction. One might quibble with how far you''ve taken the whites of that dress, but that''s all.', '2007-03-21 16:37:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(3479124, 481616, 74858, '<td valign="top">Yeah i really didnt do any editng and it was definitley a big mistake my monitor must of been brignted so i def thought that looked at least better that it is def my fault for not double checking o well theres always next time</td>', 'Yeah i really didnt do any editng and it was definitley a big mistake my monitor must of been brignted so i def thought that looked at least better that it is def my fault for not double checking o well theres always next time', '2007-03-21 16:59:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(3479125, 481080, 51386, '<td valign="top">Wow, i love the look and feel of this shot. Great post processing! I only find the light blotch around her right foot a little distracting, but very minutely. Congrats on the ribbon</td>', 'Wow, i love the look and feel of this shot. Great post processing! I only find the light blotch around her right foot a little distracting, but very minutely. Congrats on the ribbon', '2007-03-21 16:59:55.000000', NULL, 0),
